NAME='Neptune'
COVER_SUB='What a generation dreams, about 14 years in each sign.'
T=[
('1862–75 · 2026–39','Neptune in Aries, with harmonious aspects, gives a fervid imagination, sensitivity, powerful intuition and clairvoyance. Neptunian sensitivity joined to Martian energy lifts will and action toward a high ideal. A spirit of adventure and uncommon enthusiasm point toward independent professions. Dreams become mission: faith in a cause worth the effort. Karmic reading: a generation of idealist pioneers. The shadow is illusion and a crusade without a map. The lesson: an ideal needs a first practical step.'),
('1875–89 · 2039–52','Neptune in Taurus, in harmonious aspect, gives passive intellectual qualities: imagination, intuition and memory. A conservative spirit, you are an altruist and draw many useful sympathies. There is a nose for business, with income and benefit from mysterious sources, and happy intuitions in speculation. Dreams settle into the material world: art, beauty and the senses. Karmic reading: a generation learning the value of things. The shadow is illusory security and comfort as escape. The lesson: what you value should be real.'),
('1889–1902 · 2052–65','Neptune in Gemini, harmonious, gives accentuated sensitivity, ease of comprehension and assimilation, and intellectual curiosity. Imagination and good memory, with investigative gifts and an exceptional nose for business. The mind turns into a receiver of impressions, stories and rumours. Karmic reading: a generation working with words and images that move people. The shadow is confusion and half-truths. The lesson: check what you believe before you pass it on.'),
('1902–15','Neptune in Cancer, in the Moon’s house and with harmonious aspects, is a sign of sensitivity, a contemplative spirit, sensitivity and good psychic qualities. It steers toward a meditative life. Fervid imagination and deep intelligence prefer literary studies to scientific ones, and the native compensates for shyness with an inner world. Family, home and nation become something to dream about. Karmic reading: a generation healing ancestral memory. The shadow is nostalgia and dependency. The lesson: belonging is chosen as well as inherited.'),
('1915–29','Neptune in Leo, in harmonious aspect, gives good mental and psychic level, goodness and greatness of soul, and a power to involve the listener. The native is often a grey eminence. A developed artistic sense and a love of order and symmetry, with a taste for well-being and glamour. This generation saw the birth of cinema, stardom and the cult of the personality. Karmic reading: a generation learning that the heart’s radiance is real. The shadow is vanity and illusion about the self. The lesson: shine without needing a mirror.'),
('1929–43','Neptune in Virgo, in harmonious aspect, gives an easy material life. Work is free of worries and profitable, income grows and daily life is balanced. Intuition joins practical sense and excellent powers of analysis and synthesis. Dreams become service: medicine, craft, care. Karmic reading: a generation healing through useful work. The shadow is anxiety and a sense of never being enough. The lesson: perfect is the enemy of kind.'),
('1943–57','Neptune in Libra, harmonious, is a sign of intellectual elevation and harmonious relationships. Marriage makes material life more comfortable, with unions that happen in fortuitous and slightly mysterious circumstances. An idealised vision of love, art, peace and justice. Karmic reading: a generation that dreamed of harmony after upheaval. The shadow is idealising others and avoiding conflict. The lesson: a relationship is built with the real person.'),
('1957–70','Neptune in Scorpio gives intelligence and realising skills, with the gift of analysis and synthesis and an investigative dexterity. There is an attraction to the paranormal and mediumistic gifts, with medical aptitude. Professions linked to medicine are favoured. Desire, secrets and the unconscious drift into the collective mood. Karmic reading: a generation dissolving old taboos. The shadow is obsession and hidden dependency. The lesson: what is hidden also deserves light.'),
('1970–84','Neptune in Sagittarius, when harmonious, gives fervid imagination, openness of mind, kindness and intuition, but a lack of practical sense. It steers toward philosophical and religious studies. You are charitable and drawn to the mysteries of the beyond and the resolution of ultimate questions. Spiritual seeking, travel and exotic cultures come to the front. Karmic reading: a generation looking for faith without walls. The shadow is naivety and escape. The lesson: seek meaning and keep your feet on the ground.'),
('1984–98','Neptune in Capricorn, when harmonious, is a sign of reflection and concentration. You have a clear perception of situations and a disciplined, patient spirit, but a dose of egoism pushes you to seek your own well-being. It can indicate success through fortuitous causes. A powerful instinct of preservation. Dreams meet institutions: the ideal is tested against structure. Karmic reading: a generation making vision practical. The shadow is cynicism. The lesson: build what you dream, slowly.'),
('1998–2012','Neptune in Aquarius, with harmonious aspects, gives imagination, intuition and an ingenious, inventive spirit. Intellectual gifts and psychic gifts, with spiritual elevation. You find a way to overcome the problems on your path, with a revolutionary spirit. This generation grew up as the internet connected the world into a shared dream. Karmic reading: a generation of collective visionaries. The shadow is detachment and virtual escape. The lesson: community begins with presence.'),
('1848–62 · 2012–26','Neptune in Pisces, its own sign, gives accentuated sensitivity, intuition, clairvoyant gifts and a healing magnetic fluid. You are drawn to the sufferings of others and have an aptitude for the occult sciences. Excellent memory, quick learning, though study is not loved. Compassion, art, spirituality and illusion share one ocean. Karmic reading: a generation at the end of a long cycle, learning to dissolve and give back. The shadow is escapism and loss of boundaries. The lesson: compassion also protects itself.'),
]
